      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "This appears to have been slightly alleviated with the rollback, but it’s still present (which is weird, since in the previous version it wasn’t like this so the rollback should’ve fixed it).\n\n1. Go to a heavy/large world (I’m pretty sure it also happens with average worlds)\n\n2. Go to another world\n\n3. You’ll likely be sent home because you ran out of memory.\n\n4. If you clear your cache and restart, it goes away until you attempt to “jump” through multiple worlds again.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    }
  ],
  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2023-10-06T01:45:53.324Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "1. Open VRChat\n\n2. Go to a heavy world. By that I mean, for example, open-world worlds or worlds that would take a while to initialize. These worlds always took longer than usual to load, but they still worked perfectly fine after loading in in previous builds of VRChat.\n\n3. The world will try to initialize, but after a while there will be a black screen for a split second and you'll be sent to your home world with the message \"You were sent home because you ran out of memory\". If the black screen does not occur, you will instead get \"VRChat is not responding\", \"Cannot join instance\", or \"Your connection to VRChat timed out\" eventually.\n\nPS: I've seen many people mention having these issues in general, so it might not be isolated to heavy/large worlds.",
